  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Cli\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Cli\n       Program: commons-cli\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/Cli.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-cli.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Cli/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 39\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Cli-29\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n20002f7f4e971349a1c95dd3b05846c5b824b65c\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2010-06-16 08:35:18 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCLI-185\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CLI-185\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.cli.UtilTest::testStripLeadingAndTrailingQuotes\n   --> junit.framework.ComparisonFailure: expected:<foo \"bar[\"]> but was:<foo \"bar[]>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.cli.Util\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Commons CLI incorrectly stripping leading and trailing quotes\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\norg.apache.commons.cli.Parser.processArgs() calls Util.stripLeadingAndTrailingQuotes() for all argument values. IMHO this is incorrect and totally broken.\n\nIt is trivial to create a simple test for this. Output:\n\n    $ java -cp target/clitest.jar Clitest --balloo \"this is a \\\"test\\\"\"\n    Value of argument balloo is 'this is a \"test'.\n\nThe argument 'balloo' should indeed keep its trailing double quote. It is what the shell gives it, so don't try to do something clever to it.\n\nThe offending code was committed here:\n    http://svn.apache.org/viewvc?view=rev&revision=129874\nand has been there for more than 6 years (!). Why was this committed in the first place?\n\nThe fix is trivial, just get rid of Util.stripLeadingAndTrailingQuotes(), and consequently avoid calling it from Parser.processArgs().\n\nComments:\n\n[Emmanuel Bourg]: This was committed to fix CLI-22. I do agree that the quotes should not be removed.\n\n[Emmanuel Bourg]: This is a regression introduced with CLI 1.1, CLI 1.0 didn't trim the quotes.\n\n[Einar M R Rosenvinge]: Any info on when 1.3 will be out?\n\n[Emmanuel Bourg]: We just started working on CLI 1.3, it's not ready to be released yet. You can use a snapshot once the issue is fixed, but if you absolutely need a released component we might roll out a 1.2.1 bug fix release.\n\n[Einar M R Rosenvinge]: If you could release a 1.2.1 bugfix release with this fix, I'd be forever grateful. I'm depending on it for a big project. Thanks!",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.cli.Util (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.cli.Util (fixed)\n@@ -62,14 +62,10 @@\n      */\n     static String stripLeadingAndTrailingQuotes(String str)\n     {\n-        if (str.startsWith(\"\\\"\"))\n+        int length = str.length();\n+        if (length > 1 && str.startsWith(\"\\\"\") && str.endsWith(\"\\\"\") && str.substring(1, length - 1).indexOf('\"') == -1)\n         {\n-            str = str.substring(1, str.length());\n-        }\n-        int length = str.length();\n-        if (str.endsWith(\"\\\"\"))\n-        {\n-            str = str.substring(0, length - 1);\n+            str = str.substring(1, length - 1);\n         }\n         \n         return str;"
}